From 02162aabb2c5f62ec3435f17006569a4b6f0fe7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:59:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] 9678: x86: Emulate 16-bit segmented code

x86: Emulate 16-bit segmented code

Add a segment userop to the x86 emulator library for the 16-bit
languages, computing the same address as the segmentop in each 16-bit
pspec: base << 4 in real mode and base << 16 in protected mode.

Fix 16-bit far branches in ia.sinc that dropped or never set CS:
RET imm16, RETF imm16 and IRET now return to segment(CS,IP) like RET
and RETF, CALLF m16:16 assigns CS from the far pointer, and JMPF m16:16
with 16-bit addressing assigns CS and jumps to segment(CS,off).
